# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED SCHEMA ARTIFACTS — never format these.
#
# `packages/db/migrations/meta/*.json` is drizzle-kit OUTPUT, not source. Prettier
# reformats every snapshot (it collapses the multi-line `columnsFrom`/`columnsTo`
# arrays onto one line), which is semantically null — the JSON parses identically —
# but it rewrites ~60 files and makes every subsequent `pnpm db:generate` diff noisy
# against a baseline nobody intended to change. This is the migration spine
# (invariant #8: never mutate a shipped schema artifact casually), so the only safe
# posture is that a formatter never touches it at all.
#
# Hit for real on 2026-08-01: a bare `pnpm format` rewrote 735 files, 60 of them
# these snapshots, burying ~20 files of actual work pre-commit.
packages/db/migrations/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENT + SKILL DEFINITIONS — config that happens to be markdown.
#
# `.claude/agents/*.md` and `.claude/skills/**/SKILL.md` are read by tooling, not by
# people browsing docs. Prettier rewrites their emphasis markers (`*x*` -> `_x_`) and
# inserts blank lines around list blocks, producing 35 files of diff that changes no
# meaning and buries real edits to an agent's actual instructions in review.
.claude/agents/**
.claude/skills/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESUME LAYOUT SKELETONS — never format these either, for TWO independent reasons.
#
# 1. WHITESPACE IS LOAD-BEARING. Every collapsible container in these layouts is
#    written on ONE line, flush against its tags, because `:empty` does not match an
#    element holding a single space or a newline. Prettier's HTML printer breaks each
#    container across lines, which silently re-enables every section a sparse profile
#    is supposed to hide — a worker with no certifications would print a
#    "Certifications" heading with nothing under it, on a sheet they hand to an
#    employer. Nothing would fail; it would just be wrong.
#
# 2. A SHIPPED TEMPLATE VERSION IS IMMUTABLE (templates/registry.ts). A resume row
#    records the `template_id` + version it was rendered with, so reformatting
#    `classic.v3.html` edits a file that already-issued PDFs are pinned to.
#
# Measured 2026-08-28: `prettier --check` reports style issues on the shipped
# `classic.v3.html` as well as on the new `bb_trade.v1.html`, so `pnpm format` would
# have rewritten the whole directory. `bb-trade-template.test.ts` asserts the
# no-whitespace discipline independently, so a formatter run still fails CI.
apps/api/src/resume/templates/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE LEXICON'S TYPESCRIPT EMBEDDING — generator output, and the two disagree.
#
# `packages/profiling-lexicon/src/internal/data.generated.ts` is written by
# `scripts/sync-mirror.mjs`, which embeds each canonical JSON file as a string
# literal. Prettier re-quotes those literals, and `sync-mirror.mjs --check`
# then compares its own output against the reformatted file and reports the
# canonical data as STALE — which is a hard failure in two CI jobs.
#
# Hit for real on 2026-08-28: a blanket `prettier --write` over the changed-file
# list reformatted this file, `pnpm --filter @badabhai/profiling-lexicon test`
# went red with "data.generated.ts: stale — does not match .../data", and the
# only actual difference was single quotes becoming double. The generator is
# the formatter for this file; nothing else may be.
packages/profiling-lexicon/src/internal/data.generated.ts
